// The port is finished, so the spec has one impl: the Rust that answers it.
//
// It was a dual-impl porting config while the Java was still here — a
// source-impl block pinned every rule to the Konteaksta class it was read
// out of, and target-impl pinned the same rule to the Rust that replaced it.
// The Java trees were deleted once every rule had both, which retires the
// source side of the contract; the rules themselves are unchanged, and their
// markdown still lives under `docs/spec/port/sme/...` because that is where
// each one came from. The Java's final annotated state is in this
// repository's history, and its full SVN lineage is on the `svn/teaksta` and
// `svn/view` branches.
specs ({
    name teaksta,
    include (docs/spec/**/*.md),
    impls (
        {name target-impl, languages (@rust), include (src/**/*.rs crates/**/*.rs), exclude (target/**), mode @both}
    )
})
